That “Expected identifier name” error in Power Apps usually means there’s a syntax issue (not the logic itself). In your case, it’s coming from how the formula is written in Screen1.OnVisible.

Let’s fix it cleanly.


---

✅ Common Cause in Your Code

This part is the problem:

AddColumns(
    Distinct('SE Question List', Title),
    "Value",
    Result
)

👉 In Power Apps, Distinct() returns a column named Result, but sometimes the editor throws an identifier error depending on formatting or separators.


---

✅ FIXED VERSION (Safe & Working)

Use this exact format:

Clear(colHeader);

// Static columns
Collect(colHeader, {Value: "Code"});
Collect(colHeader, {Value: "Supplier"});

// Dynamic columns
Collect(
    colHeader,
    ForAll(
        Distinct('SE Question List', Title),
        {Value: Result}
    )
);


---

🔍 Why This Works

ForAll() safely converts each record into {Value: ...}

Avoids issues with AddColumns() parsing

No ambiguity → no identifier error



---

⚠️ ALSO CHECK THESE (Very Important)

1. Make sure column name is correct

If your SharePoint column is not exactly Title, fix it:

Distinct('SE Question List', 'Title')

👉 Sometimes SharePoint requires quotes.


---

2. Separator issue (PH locale)

If your app uses semicolon ; instead of comma ,, change to:

Clear(colHeader);

Collect(colHeader; {Value: "Code"});
Collect(colHeader; {Value: "Supplier"});

Collect(
    colHeader;
    ForAll(
        Distinct('SE Question List'; Title);
        {Value: Result}
    )
);

👉 This is VERY common in PH / EU regions.


---

✅ Final Working Version (Copy-Paste Safe)

If your app uses commas (,):

Clear(colHeader);

